> conversion program won't work since it would be looking at the wrong
> passwd file and putting the resulting data in the wrong place.

If you need to run a program that expects its files to
be in a specific location, use chroot. This is especially
easy when the directory you chroot to is the root of a
running system, because all the necessary binaries and
libraries are already in the appropriate locations (assunming
your root FS is mounted on /mnt):

# chroot /mnt /bin/ksh

Now you can run convuser or vipw to your heart's content.

Take care,

